+# v2.0.1 implementation and verification report
+
+Date: 5 November 2026.
+
+Historical baseline: the [focused remediation report](v2.0.1-remediation-report.md) supersedes this report's verification totals and native stop-mechanism description following correction of the four independent review findings.
+
+Authority: [Final v2.0.1 implementation specification](../plans/v2.0.1-implementation-specification.md). That specification was preserved during implementation.
+
+Status: Implementation complete and locally verified on Linux. **Release acceptance remains pending Windows/macOS native verification and execution of the configured CI matrix.** No release, publication, commit, or push was performed.
+
+## Implementation completed
+
+The work followed the specification's sequence, with relevant tests run after each component.
+
+| Sequence | Delivered behavior | Verification during implementation |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| 1. Validation and discovery foundations | Complete ASCII decimal port parsing; checked command results retaining stderr/status; typed discovery errors; cancellable collection budget; prioritized discovery queue; portable test runner. | Initial 4 foundation tests passed. |
+| 2. Platform discovery | Required listener enumeration fails explicitly; optional process metadata remains best effort; Windows snapshots are validated; deadline expiry preserves enumerated rows; late work cannot publish caches. | Expanded suite: 15 tests passed. |
+| 3. Captured-target actions | TUI actions capture PID/port; CLI kill retains first-discovered listener semantics; fresh validation before initial and forced stops; alive/exited/unknown liveness; incomplete and unverified stops fail accurately. | Expanded suite: 21 tests passed. |
+| 4. TUI selection and refresh | PID/port selection survives sorting and refresh; refresh requests coalesce; action validation uses the same coordinator; stale/unavailable states and action errors persist correctly; repeated pending actions are ignored. | Expanded suite: 26 tests passed, including rendered Ink tests. |
+| 5. CLI error contract | One error boundary covers explicit commands and non-TTY fallback; diagnostics go to stderr; JSON schema is unchanged; invalid arguments/help/version never construct a backend. | Expanded suite: 29 tests passed; initial 3 built CLI integration tests passed. |
+| 6. Version, documentation, and CI | Application and root lockfile versions are 2.0.1; CLI/TUI share one version source; current documentation and history are updated; cross-platform checks are configured. | Version-consistency regression added; historical v2.0.0 statements retained; dependency versions unchanged. |
+| 7. Final verification | Native fixture replay, kernel liveness classifications, snapshot isolation, forced-stop failures, command arguments with spaces, and newline/tab rejection are covered. | Final results below. |
+
+Stopping a process still affects all of its ports. A released listener with a live process is an incomplete stop, exits 1, and does not trigger forced termination. Only confirmed exit is reported as stopped. Successful JSON retains `port`, `pid`, `command`, `projectName`, `framework`, `memoryKB`, and `uptime`.
+
+## Affected components
+
+- `src/validation.ts`, `src/discovery.ts`, and `src/system.ts`: strict parsing, checked execution, deadlines/cancellation, diagnostics, and snapshot coordination.
+- `src/backends/types.ts`, `src/backends/common.ts`, `src/backends/unix.ts`, and `src/backends/windows.ts`: validated listener collection, optional metadata, guarded termination, and liveness outcomes.
+- `src/ports.ts` and `src/types.ts`: internal listener targets, isolated snapshots, staged stable-process metadata, and target-specific actions.
+- `src/project.ts`: cache writes participate in collection publication; project/framework detection rules are unchanged.
+- `src/tui.tsx` and `src/tui-state.ts`: target selection, coalesced refresh, stale/unavailable state, duplicate-action suppression, and unmount handling.
+- `src/cli.tsx`, `src/commands.tsx`, and `src/version.ts`: executable entry point, testable command handling, output contracts, and shared version.
+- `tests/`, `scripts/test.mjs`, and `scripts/native-smoke.mjs`: automated regressions, portable test discovery, and owned-server native verification.
+- `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: Linux/macOS/Windows Node 24 matrix and Linux Node 22.18.0, including native smoke artifacts.
+- `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `README.md`, `USER_MANUAL.md`, `index.html`, and `PROJECT_HISTORY.md`: test scripts, version metadata, and corrected user-facing behavior.
+
+No runtime or development dependencies were added or upgraded. The lockfile changes only the two application/root-package version entries. Framework detection, editor precedence, public commands, TCP-only collection, and the existing one-second escalation interval remain unchanged except for the specified guards.
+
+## Completed local verification
+
+Environment: Linux kernel `7.0.0-42-generic`; Node `v24.21.0`; npm `11.19.0`; `lsof 4.95.0`; `ps` from procps-ng `4.0.4`.
+
+| Check | Final local result |
+| --- | --- |
+| `npm ci` | Passed; clean install, 119 packages installed, audit reported 0 vulnerabilities. |
+| `npm run typecheck` | Passed. |
+| `npm test` | **35 passed**, 0 failed/cancelled/skipped. |
+| `npm run build` | Passed; ESM executable and declarations generated. |
+| `npm run test:integration` | **3 passed**, 0 failed/cancelled/skipped; executes the built CLI using test-only platform executables. |
+| `node dist/cli.js --help` | Passed; command help printed without discovery. |
+| `node dist/cli.js --version` | Passed; printed `2.0.1`. |
+| `npm run test:native` | **4 native checks passed**; details below. |
+| Live Linux terminal | Passed: startup, automatic refresh, manual `r`, sort `s`, retained selection, and clean `q` exit with status 0. No stop or GUI-launch shortcut was used. |
+| `git diff --check` | Passed after whitespace cleanup. |
+
+The final integration run included malformed ports with suffixes, fractions, exponent notation, surrounding whitespace, non-ASCII digits, tabs, and CR/LF. Source-level command tests cover the full specified argument matrix, boundaries, leading zeros, and missing arguments before backend construction.
+
+The unit suite exercises both backend implementations on Linux using deterministic command fixtures. This is **fixture coverage of Windows behavior**, not native Windows verification. Tests also render the actual Ink component using synthetic terminal streams and mock actions, without another testing dependency.
+
+### Native Linux checks and evidence
+
+The native smoke script created a target server with IPv4/IPv6 listeners and a separate owned sentinel server. It refused to invoke port-based termination unless every discovered row on the target port belonged to its target child. Only test-owned child processes were signaled or cleaned up; unrelated processes were not terminated.
+
+The four checks passed:
+
+1. The owned target appeared in built CLI JSON, static table, and detailed check output.
+2. Native `lsof` valid IPv4/IPv6, controlled no-match, and invalid-option signatures were captured and verified.
+3. The CLI stopped the owned target successfully while the owned sentinel survived.
+4. Successful discovery reported the released port free, removed the exited target, and continued reporting the sentinel.
+
+Raw commands, stdout, stderr, exit statuses, and platform/tool details are recorded in [native-linux.json](native-linux.json). A separate stable copy of the captured `lsof` fixtures is retained in [the regression fixtures](../../tests/fixtures/linux-lsof.json), replayed on every test host.
+
+Browser/editor launch behavior, including paths with spaces, was verified through command-runner stubs. No real browser or editor was launched. Shared-port and forced-escalation scenarios use fixtures/mock probes and signals; the real native stop check exercised normal termination of an owned child.
+
+## Specification reconciliation and deviations
+
+There are no additional product features or intentional scope departures. The following implementation choices and verification limitations are recorded explicitly:
+
+| Item | Resolution |
+| --- | --- |
+| Native Linux no-match signature | This environment emits paired `can't stat() overlay/nsfs file system` / `Output information may be incomplete.` warnings with both successful listener queries and a controlled no-match exit 1. Section 7.3 explicitly permits a verified platform-specific classification. The implementation accepts only empty stdout/status 1 with those exact warning forms on Linux and retains a visibility warning. Extra/unknown diagnostics still fail; macOS does not inherit the Linux exception. |
+| Small project module change | `getPackageContext` accepts an optional collection context and stages cache writes so late enrichment cannot publish. This is required deadline handling, not cache invalidation or a change to project/framework detection. |
+| Windows query separation | Required listener enumeration is separated from optional batched process/CIM enrichment so a stalled enrichment query cannot lose already discovered listeners. No general performance redesign was added. |
+| Unix liveness | Uses the kernel-backed Node `process.kill(pid, 0)` probe so numeric `ESRCH`/`EPERM` errors distinguish absence from permission outcomes. It sends no terminating signal. Other errors remain unknown. |
+| Command test seam | Command handling was extracted into `src/commands.tsx`, leaving the executable entry point small. This permits proof that parsing/help/version do not create a backend, without production test switches or extra runtime dependencies. |
+| Restricted-process environment | Initial restricted test execution and clean installation encountered `EPERM` while launching/capturing child processes. Both were rerun with the required process access and passed. This did not require a product-code workaround. |
+| Native/CI verification | Windows/macOS and Node 22.18.0 were unavailable locally. Their checks remain pending; CI configuration is provided but was not dispatched or observed in this work. AC-12 is therefore pending. |
+
+The original three-second refresh interval, Unix SIGTERM/conditional SIGKILL sequence, Windows Stop-Process/conditional forced-stop sequence, and successful JSON schema are retained. The authoritative specification's incomplete-stop and unknown-verification exceptions are implemented and documented as intentional compatibility corrections.
+
+## Acceptance coverage and pending release checks
+
+| Criteria | Evidence/status |
+| --- | --- |
+| AC-01–AC-04: exact targets, selection, guarded stop | Covered locally by action/shared-port/lifecycle tests, rendered TUI tests, and the owned Linux stop check; native Windows/macOS confirmation remains pending. |
+| AC-05–AC-07: discovery outcomes, optional metadata, CLI streams | Covered locally by Unix/Windows fixtures, deadline tests, native Linux discovery, and built CLI integration tests. |
+| AC-08–AC-09: stale data and coordination | Covered locally by rendered TUI, queue/selection/deadline/isolation tests, late-publication tests, and Linux live terminal refresh/sort checks. |
+| AC-10–AC-11: strict arguments and version | Covered locally by parser, source CLI, built CLI, package/version consistency, and documentation checks. |
+| AC-12: full platform verification | **Pending.** No claim of completed cross-platform release acceptance. |
+
+Before release:
+
+- Run the configured CI matrix on Linux/macOS/Windows Node 24 and Linux Node 22.18.0; retain its results and native JSON artifacts.
+- On macOS, verify native listener enumeration/stop/free-port checks and capture actual `lsof` IPv4/IPv6, no-match, and diagnostic signatures. Resolve only explicitly verified signature differences, as required by the specification.
+- On Windows, verify actual PowerShell discovery, payload serialization, metadata permissions, missing-tool/failed-query diagnostics, liveness, and owned-server stop behavior. The backend uses the documented [Get-NetTCPConnection cmdlet](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/module/nettcpip/get-nettcpconnection?view=windowsserver2025-ps); fixtures do not establish native cmdlet behavior.
+- Complete live terminal startup/refresh/selection/quit checks on macOS and Windows, plus harmless command-runner or executable-stub checks for browser/editor actions with spaced paths.
+- Record every unexecuted or failed check as pending/failed; mark release acceptance complete only after all required platform checks pass.
+
+Known retained limitations: PID reuse and validation-to-signal races are not eliminated; cwd/project metadata remains cached and best effort; OS permissions can hide listeners. The fixed-width TUI can wrap in narrow terminals, as observed in the local 80-column terminal; responsive layout remains outside this patch's scope. The project history deliberately labels v2.0.1 unreleased until platform acceptance and release work are complete.
